    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always had a strong connection with mathematics, especially since it’s one of my favorite subjects. I enjoy solving problems and seeing how patterns emerge. Even with my upper secondary education, I find math practical and intuitive—especially in economics and everyday life. I see it as a tool for understanding the world, not just abstract rules.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. My low neuroticism and calm mindset mean I rarely feel anxious about math. When I face a tough problem, I take deep breaths and break it down. I’ve learned to approach math like a puzzle—each step is manageable. My Buddhist beliefs also help me stay patient and non-judgmental, which reduces pressure.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used an AI app to practice algebra and calculus problems. It gave me instant feedback and explained steps clearly. It was especially helpful when I was stuck on second-order equations. The interface was intuitive, and I appreciated how it adapted to my mistakes. It felt like a supportive tutor, not a replacement.",
