    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, explain concepts in simple language, and adapt to students’ pace. They can generate practice problems, clarify misconceptions, and even simulate classroom discussions. For students like me who learn best through examples, LLMs make math more accessible and less intimidating—especially in diverse classrooms."
